# Pairs with SagaFallbackOnlyAcrossFull. A commit terminal is appended before
# the decision is recorded (invariant I1 broken), so the window holds a commit
# terminal d0 does not explain, and the increment falls back to fail safe.
MODULE: SagaFallbackOnlyAcrossFullTerminalBeforeDecision
TARGET: SagaFallbackOnlyAcrossFull
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a commit terminal precedes its recorded decision
PERTURBS: Terminal

--- FIND
    /\ dec # "none"
    /\ x \notin Terminated
    /\ wal' = [wal EXCEPT ![TermPart[x]] =
                 Append(@, [k |-> IF dec = "committed" THEN "commit" ELSE "abort", x |-> x])]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: a commit terminal before any decision.
    /\ dec # "aborted"
    /\ x \notin Terminated
    /\ wal' = [wal EXCEPT ![TermPart[x]] = Append(@, [k |-> "commit", x |-> x])]
--- END
